\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Cell ranks and physical labels}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The 4 right-module generators in \ref{fdip-00ZR}
label the vertex, two edges and face. The universal
commutant is restricted to the
[declared geometric and internal right actions](fdip-00VK)
and requires commutation for every link assignment.
It does not classify every endomorphism commuting with
one fixed kernel. These module ranks are not taste or
color counts; the operator comparison in \ref{fdip-00W9}
keeps these interpretations separate.}

\p{The dressed pair in \ref{fdip-00ZR} is an algebraic
observable with a specified path, field order and
coefficient functional. A physical hadron interpretation
or a QCD construction would require further data and
results; neither follows from these exact finite means.}
